1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:17,212
All five stories from lessons six to ten — always four pictures and a full model story in the past tense. Plus twelve phrases that get you through any story, and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and tell it out loud!

2
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:29,054
How does task 3 work? You get four pictures that together tell one story. You tell what happened — in the past tense. You can get ten points for this task.

3
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:53,652
The most important thing is the past tense. Man: šel, měl, byl. Woman: šla, měla, byla. Several people: šli, měli, byli. And when you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem: šel jsem, šla jsem. Now we go through all five stories. First tell it yourself, then you hear the model.

4
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:56,799
Story 6: The lost key.

5
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,819
What happened to Mr Vlk yesterday?

6
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:13,700
Yesterday evening Mr Vlk was walking home from work.

7
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,130
He was tired and looking forward to dinner.

8
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:18,800
When he got to the door, he looked for his key.

9
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,657
He looked in his pocket and his bag, but it wasn't there.

10
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:23,667
He had probably left it at work.

11
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:25,625
Mr Vlk didn't know what to do.

12
00:01:25,833 --> 00:01:27,767
In the end he called a locksmith.

13
00:01:27,967 --> 00:01:29,897
The locksmith arrived half an hour later.

14
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:31,800
He opened the door in five minutes.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,164
Mr Vlk had to pay him eight hundred crowns and was sad.

16
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:38,167
Story 7: At the doctor's.

17
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:40,059
What happened to Olga yesterday?

18
00:01:52,767 --> 00:01:54,856
Yesterday morning Olga didn't feel well.

19
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:58,390
She was lying in bed with a headache and a fever.

20
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,095
She couldn't go to work.

21
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,323
She called the surgery and made an appointment with the doctor.

22
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:06,033
The nurse told her to come at ten o'clock.

23
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:07,853
The doctor examined Olga.

24
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:11,133
She told her she had flu and wrote her a prescription.

25
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:13,225
Then Olga went to the pharmacy.

26
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:15,161
She bought medicine and tea.

27
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:17,724
At home she lay down and rested all day.

28
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:20,540
Story 8: A working day.

29
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:22,391
What did Ivan do yesterday?

30
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,290
Yesterday Ivan got up at four in the morning.

31
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,659
He got dressed quickly, drank a coffee and went to work.

32
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:42,631
He works in a big warehouse.

33
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:45,733
All morning he loaded heavy boxes into a lorry.

34
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:48,200
The work was hard but it went well.

35
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,700
At noon he had lunch with colleagues in the canteen.

36
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,628
He had soup and goulash.

37
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:54,395
They talked about football.

38
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,484
In the evening Ivan was very tired.

39
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,467
He rested at home on the sofa and watched TV.

40
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:02,097
Story 9: At the office.

41
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,020
What did Mr Kovač do yesterday?

42
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:20,063
Yesterday Mr Kovač went to the office because he needed a new document.

43
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:21,951
There were a lot of people at the office.

44
00:03:22,167 --> 00:03:25,000
He had to wait in the queue for a long time, almost an hour.

45
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,020
Then he filled in a form.

46
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:30,388
He wrote his name, address and date of birth there.

47
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:33,461
He didn't know some things, so he asked the clerk.

48
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:35,767
Then he had to have a photo taken for the new document.

49
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:37,658
The photo was ready right away.

50
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:40,167
Finally the clerk gave him a confirmation.

51
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:43,258
She told him he could collect the document in a month.

52
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:45,781
Story 10: Christmas.

53
00:03:46,067 --> 00:03:48,400
What did the Petrenko family do on Christmas Eve?

54
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,053
On Christmas Eve the Petrenko family was at home all day.

55
00:04:04,267 --> 00:04:06,333
In the morning they decorated the Christmas tree.

56
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:09,167
The children put baubles and lights on the tree.

57
00:04:09,367 --> 00:04:11,133
In the afternoon they baked Christmas cookies.

58
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:14,663
Mum made the dough and the children cut out little stars.

59
00:04:14,867 --> 00:04:16,567
The whole flat smelled wonderful.

60
00:04:16,767 --> 00:04:19,451
In the evening they ate carp with potato salad.

61
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:21,623
It was a traditional Czech dinner.

62
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:24,525
Then they went to the tree and unwrapped the presents.

63
00:04:24,733 --> 00:04:26,867
The children got new toys and books.

64
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:29,600
Everyone was very happy and in the evening they sang carols.

65
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:35,342
Now twelve phrases that work for any story. Listen and repeat out loud.

66
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:38,067
Yesterday morning I got up at seven.

67
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:42,821
First I had breakfast.

68
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:47,853
Then I went to work.

69
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:52,667
Suddenly it started to rain.

70
00:04:55,867 --> 00:04:57,393
In the end we went home.

71
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,051
He was tired because he worked a lot.

72
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:08,626
They had no umbrella, so they were wet.

73
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,333
The weather was nice.

74
00:05:16,533 --> 00:05:18,364
In the afternoon she went to the police.

75
00:05:21,567 --> 00:05:23,200
Marie had a birthday.

76
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,133
Mr Tichý had to stay at home.

77
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:32,967
In the evening friends came.

78
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:39,225
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

79
00:05:42,433 --> 00:05:50,069
Correct: Olga ležela v posteli. Tell the story in the past tense: ležela, šla, koupila.

80
00:05:53,767 --> 00:06:04,633
Correct: Marie pekla dort. Woman: -la. Man: -l. Several people: -li.

81
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:14,606
Correct: Včera jsem šel do práce. When you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem.

82
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:30,114
Correct: Ráno balili věci a potom přijelo auto. Don’t describe the pictures. Tell a story with linking words: nejdřív, potom, nakonec.

83
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:44,624
Correct: Jel na kole do práce. Najednou vyběhl pes a on spadl. Say two or three sentences for each picture: who, where, what and why.

84
00:06:45,833 --> 00:07:05,407
Summary. First: tell the story in the past tense. Second: link your sentences — nejdřív, potom, nakonec. Third: two or three sentences for each picture. And fourth: watch the gender — on šel, ona šla.

85
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:16,060
Which story is the hardest for you? Write it in the comments — and try to write the first two sentences in the past tense. And if the video helped, give it a like.

86
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:33,874
On the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website you can practise all stories for free — it listens and checks your past tense. Link in the description. Tomorrow: big review of Speaking task 4. Subscribe so you don’t miss anything.
